# Paged KV: the per-side decode-READ kernel, PLUS (fable-review follow-up, same task,
# see the later addenda below) the write-kernel split and guard/test hardening it needed
# (u8 keys / i4 values)
#
# docs/design-m8-asymmetric-kv.md, the design this task's own binding spec named. Ships the
# kernel-source half the design's scope verdict called "a bounded macro de-coupling, not a
# tiling rewrite" for exactly one direction - key>=8bit / value 4bit (u8-K/i4-V) - on the DECODE
# fast path only (paged_attention_opt.cpp/.cl's SINGLE_TOKEN stage). Applied against the pinned
# runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of patches/0001-0009 (0008 = VALUE_CACHE_
# PRECISION config plumbing this kernel reads; 0009 = the micro-SDPA decline, whose own logic is
# UNCHANGED by this patch - see "prefill" below).
#
# Scope note (fable-review follow-up, added later in the same task, see the numbered addenda
# below): "DECODE ONLY" above describes this patch's ORIGINAL scope - the READ-side kernel
# split (§1/§2). It stopped being the whole truth once the write-kernel split (§7) landed in
# the same patch: pa_kv_cache_update_ref.cl is ONE compiled program reachable from every write
# stage (decode/2nd-token AND both prefill stages), so its IS_INT4_K/IS_INT4_V split had to be,
# and is, consistent across all three - not decode-only. The dual-nibble dispatch fix in §1 also
# touches the MULTI_TOKENS stage's DispatchDataFunc, not just SINGLE_TOKEN's, though it is
# "fixed for consistency, not exercised" there per §1's own text. What IS still decode-only is
# what actually SERVES asymmetric precision end-to-end: prefill still declines to the OCL
# fallback (§3, patches/0009's guard, unchanged) rather than serving u8:i4 on micro-SDPA or the
# opt kernel's own MULTI_TOKENS stage - so "decode serves, prefill still falls back" (§3's own
# phrase) remains the accurate summary of what a caller observes, even though the write-side fix
# is not decode-scoped internally.
#
# ---- 1. THE JIT SPLIT (paged_attention_opt.cpp) ----
#
# make_uint4_kv_cache_jit_constants() and PagedAttentionGeneratorBase::get_jit_constants() used
# to derive every packing constant from one shared `kv_cache_dt = get_kv_cache_precision()`
# (key-side only), so a compiled kernel instance was always either "both operands packed" or
# "both unpacked" - never split. IS_INT4_COMPRESSED is retired; IS_INT4_K = is_i4_u4(get_kv_
# cache_precision()) and IS_INT4_V = is_i4_u4(get_value_cache_precision()) now gate their own
# operand independently: PACKED_K_HEAD_SIZE / PACKED_ADJUSTED_K_HEAD_SIZE / PACKED_K_BLOCK_SIZE
# emit iff IS_INT4_K; PACKED_V_HEAD_SIZE / PACKED_ADJUSTED_V_HEAD_SIZE iff IS_INT4_V.
# ADJUSTED_K_HEAD_SIZE / ADJUSTED_PAGED_ATTENTION_BLOCK_SIZE / IS_KEY_BY_CHANNEL now select on
# IS_INT4_K (u8-K takes the same unpacked "+scale_zp" arm i8-K always took - the formula was
# already int4-agnostic there); ADJUSTED_V_HEAD_SIZE never distinguished i4 from i8 to begin
# with (it counts adjusted *elements*, not bytes - PACKED_V_HEAD_SIZE carries the bitwidth), so
# it only needed its own scale/zp size (from the VALUE port, not the KEY port SCALE_ZP_SIZE_PER_
# TOKEN was reading before). USE_DUAL_NIBBLE_V_OPT already keyed on value-side packing once
# nested inside `if (is_int4_v)` - unchanged in effect, per the design's own read. IS_KV_
# COMPRESSED (key-layout, both-sides-quantised flag) stays as-is, per design §1.
#
# One thing NOT in the design doc, found while implementing it: can_use_dual_nibble_v() - which
# decides whether the SG_SCALE_FACTOR / workgroup-dispatch math treats V as packed - was called
# at all four of its call sites (the base get_jit_constants, and the SingleToken/GQASingleToken/
# MultiTokens DispatchDataFunc lambdas) with kv_cache_dt (the KEY precision), even though dual-
# nibble is entirely a VALUE-side read optimization. This was silently correct only because K and
# V were always mirrored pre-0008; for u8-K/i4-V it would have sized the dispatch for an
# UNPACKED V (using full v_head_size) while the kernel body - correctly, after the JIT split
# above - expects PACKED_V_HEAD_SIZE. That is a workgroup-size mismatch, not a missing
# optimization, and it would not have shown up as a compile error. Fixed at all four sites to key
# on get_value_cache_precision() instead. This is why the design's "no dispatch change" claim
# holds for the shipped direction: it holds once this conflation is fixed, not before.
#
# ---- 2. THE .cl DIVERGENCE (paged_attention_opt.cl) ----
#
# Renamed the K-only occurrences of the old shared gate (the by-channel branch and the K-unpack
# i4-nibble-vs-i8-BLOCK_READN split - 2 conditional sites, plus their matching #else/#endif
# comments) to IS_INT4_K, and the V-only occurrences (the per-token scale-pointer branch and the
# two V-unpack nibble paths - 5 conditional sites, plus comments) to IS_INT4_V. The one site that
# mixed both operands in one #if/#else (the phys_adjusted_k/v_head_size and phys_k/v_head_size
# locals) was split into two independent #if/#else blocks, one per operand (1 IS_INT4_K + 1
# IS_INT4_V), rather than renamed in place - 9 conditional gate sites total. For u8-K/i4-V specifically,
# every V code path (dual-nibble dispatch, PACKED_V_*, the two V-unpack arms) is now BYTE-
# IDENTICAL to the i4:i4 case - untouched by this patch; only K flips from the packed nibble-
# unpack arm to the pre-existing i8 BLOCK_READN arm. No new loops, no dispatch-math edits beyond
# the can_use_dual_nibble_v() fix in §1.
#
# ---- 3. PREFILL: UNCHANGED, STILL DECLINED ----
#
# patches/0009's supports_micro_sdpa() decline (is_i4_u4(key) != is_i4_u4(value) -> false) is not
# touched by this patch and needs no change: it already declines micro-SDPA for u8-K/i4-V
# correctly, because is_i4_u4(u8)=false != is_i4_u4(i4)=true. Prefill therefore still falls back
# off micro exactly as it did before this patch - this patch does not make prefill serve u8:i4,
# and does not attempt to. The other prefill path this generation carries, PagedAttentionSDPAOpt
# GeneratorMultiToken ("sdpa_opt" kernel, sdpa_base.cpp/sdpa_gen_opt.hpp) - a SEPARATE kernel
# from paged_attention_opt.cl, not touched by this patch - was read (not fixed): it hard-codes
# IS_KV_COMPRESSED=0 for its own paged multi-token stage regardless of config, so it already
# cannot express KV compression at all on this path, pre-existing and orthogonal to this patch.
# design §3's own instruction stands: "do not silently send u8-K/i4-V onto the sdpa_opt multi-
# token path unaudited" - it is unaudited, and this patch does not route anything onto it that
# was not already reachable before.
#
# ---- 4. THE CONFIG-LEVEL GUARD (execution_config.cpp, relaxing patches/0008's finalize check) ----
#
# patches/0008/0009 refused EVERY key/value bitwidth mismatch at ExecutionConfig::finalize()
# time: `(key.bitwidth()==4) == (value.bitwidth()==4)` had to hold, full stop. That assert is
# narrowed to `!(key.bitwidth()==4 && value.bitwidth()!=4)` - i.e. only a 4-bit KEY paired with a
# non-4-bit VALUE (i4-K/u8-V, the harder direction design §2 declined to attempt - it would move
# V off the dual-nibble dispatch, which does touch workgroup sizing) is still refused.
#
# SERVED vs REFUSED, after this patch (key : value, both already through the u8->i8/i4->u4
# storage-convention swap in finalize_impl):
#   i8:i8, u8:u8         SERVED  (unchanged, symmetric, pre-existing)
#   i4:i4 (u4:u4)         SERVED  (unchanged, symmetric, pre-existing)
#   i8:i4 / u8:i4 (u4)    SERVED  (NEW - this patch, DECODE ONLY; prefill still declines to the
#                                  fallback per §3, unaudited/unpriced by this task)
#   i4:i8 / i4:u8 (etc.)  REFUSED (unchanged - "genuinely harder", design §2, not attempted)
#
