# ---- 6. BUG A2: EXPLICIT SIGNED VALUE READ (paged_attention_opt.cl, M8 follow-up task) ----
#
# Independent of, and in addition to, patches/0008's Round 6 config-layer fix (execution_config.
# cpp - see that patch's own header): the non-4-bit value dequant in this same kernel
# (PagedAttentionGeneratorSingleToken's SINGLE_TOKEN body, both the main per-partition V loop and
# the trailing "leftovers" loop) read the value cache PORT type directly
# (`convert_half(value_packed)`, no signed cast) where the KEY dequant, on the same stage, is
# immune to its own port's declared signedness because the key port is unconditionally normalized
# to i8 upstream. The value cache is unconditionally SIGNED i8 storage in the non-4-bit case
# (pa_kv_cache_update_ref.cl's quantize_and_save_per_token, INT8 arm - signed zero-point,
# convert_char_rte), independent of what the value port happens to be declared as. An explicit
# `(char)` reinterpretation, added at both sites, makes this read correct regardless of the
# port's declared type - config-layer correctness (0008's Round 6) already keeps that port at i8
# today, but this closes the same invariant on the kernel side too, so a future config regression
# in this specific spot would not silently reopen the bug this round's own diagnosis found.
#
# ---- 7. BUG B: THE WRITE KERNEL SPLIT (pa_kv_cache_update_ref.cl + paged_attention_opt.cpp,
#          M8 follow-up task - RESOLVES the "KV-cache WRITE kernel" item in GATES OWED above) ----
#
# The GATES OWED item above ("The KV-cache WRITE kernel ... is NOT touched by this patch") is
# CLOSED by this task. Root cause, measured -nan at output[0] on
# paged_attention_asymmetric_kv_test.decode_serves_u8_key_i4_value (§5's own new test, until this
# fix): KVCacheUpdateGenerator::get_jit_constants (paged_attention_opt.cpp) derived every packing
# constant - INCLUDING whether make_uint4_kv_cache_jit_constants() (the function that emits
# IS_INT4_V/PACKED_V_HEAD_SIZE/PACKED_ADJUSTED_V_HEAD_SIZE/USE_DUAL_NIBBLE_V_OPT) is even called
# at all - from kv_cache_dt (the KEY-side config value) alone. For u8-K/i4-V,
# is_i4_u4(kv_cache_dt=i8/u8) is false, so that function was never called: IS_INT4_V stayed
# undefined for the WRITE kernel's compilation (OpenCL's preprocessor treats an undefined macro
# as 0 in #if, so this compiled silently rather than failing), and the write kernel kept writing
# the value cache UNPACKED every decode step regardless of what VALUE_CACHE_PRECISION actually
# resolved to - while the already-fixed READ kernel (§1/§2 above) expected PACKED value bytes
# whenever IS_INT4_V is true. A stride mismatch on the value cache, not a missing optimization -
# exactly what GATES OWED named as "the actual, load-bearing reason u8-K/i4-V is not yet safe to
# serve end-to-end."
#
# Fix: split KVCacheUpdateGenerator::get_jit_constants and pa_kv_cache_update_ref.cl's ~22
# IS_INT4_COMPRESSED sites into independent IS_INT4_K / IS_INT4_V gates, exactly mirroring §1/§2's
# read-side split:
#   - paged_attention_opt.cpp: KVCacheUpdateGenerator now computes is_int4_k/is_int4_v
#     independently (get_kv_cache_precision()/get_value_cache_precision()), calls
#     make_uint4_kv_cache_jit_constants() whenever EITHER side is 4-bit (that function already
#     gates its own K/V halves independently, per §1), and derives K's ADJUSTED_K_HEAD_SIZE/
#     ADJUSTED_PAGED_ATTENTION_BLOCK_SIZE/NUM_K_HEAD_SIZE_PARTITIONS from is_int4_k only. One
#     latent bug fixed as a side effect: ADJUSTED_V_HEAD_SIZE previously added the KEY's own
#     scales_zp_size unconditionally (harmless only while K and V were always mirrored); it now
#     uses V's own scales_zp_size, independent of K's port type.
#   - pa_kv_cache_update_ref.cl: the shared write helper quantize_and_save_per_token - previously
#     ONE function body, called from both the key call site (out_data_pitch = block size,
#     head-major) and the value call site (out_data_pitch = 1, token-major) under one
#     IS_INT4_COMPRESSED - cannot express two different compile-time behaviors for the same
#     compiled program from a single shared body, so it is now two instantiations:
#     quantize_and_save_per_token_k (gated IS_INT4_K, called only from key sites) and
#     quantize_and_save_per_token_v (gated IS_INT4_V, called only from value sites), bodies
#     otherwise identical. Every other IS_INT4_COMPRESSED site in this file - the BY_CHANNEL-only
#     helpers (COMP_K_OFFSET, quantize_and_save_by_channel_block_with_requantize[_int4],
#     quantize_and_save_by_channel_prefill, all key-only by construction - BY_CHANNEL is never a
#     value-side layout), the kernel's top-of-function phys_*_head_size block (split into two
#     independent #if blocks, one per operand, mirroring §1's read-side fix to the same kind of
#     site), and the three write stages this kernel body inlines (decode/2nd-token, prefill
#     block-full, prefill block-partial - all THREE, not just decode: unlike the read side, this
#     is one compiled kernel body reachable from every stage, so a K/V split has to be consistent
#     across all of them for physical cache layout to stay self-consistent between a block written
#     during prefill and the same block read during decode) - now reads IS_INT4_K where it writes
#     the key cache and IS_INT4_V where it writes the value cache. Two "block is full" / "block
#     partial" BY_CHANNEL sections that used to pick a combined "both int4" or "both int8" branch
#     as a single unit are restructured into independently-gated K-write-selection followed by
#     independently-gated V-per-token-loop, rather than merely renamed in place - the combined
#     form cannot express K unpacked / V packed at all, renaming alone would not have fixed it.
#
