# ---- 9. THE f16-PAIRING GUARD FIX (execution_config.cpp, fable-review follow-up F2) ----
#
# The guard narrowed in §4 above - `!(key.bitwidth()==4 && value.bitwidth()!=4)` - checks
# bitwidth() alone, so it silently ADMITTED f16:i4, f16:u8, and u8:f16, none of which this
# generation can serve: get_kv_compressed() (paged_attention_opt.cpp) decides whether the
# paged-attention path treats the cache as compressed at all from the KEY port alone; the value
# pool's physical shape is sized for an INT precision (packed-u4 or plain-int8) on both sides; and
# the write kernel (§7 above) writes a fixed INT stride into whatever pool got allocated. An f16
# side paired with any INT side is a shape mismatch this generation has no code path for, not a
# missing optimization - the same class of real corruption hole the bitwidth()==4 check already
# guards against for 4-bit mismatches, just an f16-shaped instance of it the original check didn't
# cover (f16's bitwidth is 16, never 4, so the "key is 4-bit" arm never fires for any f16 side,
# healthy or not). Fixed by refusing whenever exactly one side resolves to f16 - a 4-bit value
# still requires an 8-bit-INT key (unchanged), and an f16 side now requires f16 on BOTH sides.
# Loud finalize-time refusal, same style and message shape as the existing guard, naming both
# resolved precisions.
#
# SERVED vs REFUSED, updated (adds the f16 rows §4's table didn't have):
#   i8:i8, u8:u8, f16:f16   SERVED  (unchanged, symmetric)
#   i4:i4 (u4:u4)            SERVED  (unchanged, symmetric)
#   i8:i4 / u8:i4 (u4)       SERVED  (decode only, §1/§2; prefill still falls back, §3)
#   i4:i8 / i4:u8 (etc.)     REFUSED (unchanged - "genuinely harder", design §2, not attempted)
#   f16:i4, f16:u8, u8:f16,
#   i4:f16, i8:f16 (etc.)    REFUSED (NEW here, F2 - an f16 side requires f16 on both sides;
#                                     this generation has no INT/f16-mixed cache code path)
#
# ---- 10. THE PA_KV_REORDER GUARD (pa_kv_reorder.cpp, fable-review follow-up F3) ----
#
# pa_kv_reorder.cpp (ocl_v2)'s PaKVReorderGenerator::get_jit_constants and its kernel,
# pa_kv_cache_reorder_ref.cl, gate VALUE-cache row moves on the SAME collapsed
# IS_INT4_COMPRESSED derived from desc->cache_dt (the KEY side) alone that §7 above had to split
# in the write-update kernel - Bug B's mechanism, in a THIRD kernel this task had not looked at.
# UNREACHABLE in arcint today: no PaKVReorder nodes are ever constructed in the pipeline arcint
# runs (cache-block rotation / reorder fusion is not part of that pipeline), so this is not a live
# serving bug, and it does not contradict anything this patch actually SERVES. It does contradict
# this patch's own "read and write agree on layout for every pairing this guard permits" claim
# (§7 above) taken as a whole-plugin statement rather than a paged_attention_opt-kernel-scoped one
# - worth naming precisely rather than leaving implied. Fix, proportionate to a code path nothing
# reaches (NOT the full IS_INT4_K/IS_INT4_V split §7 did for the write-update kernel - that would
# not be proportionate here): PaKVReorderGenerator::get_jit_constants now reads
# VALUE_CACHE_PRECISION independently and asserts is_i4_u4(key) == is_i4_u4(value), refusing loud
# at JIT-constant-generation time rather than silently moving value rows at the wrong (key-shaped)
# stride if this generator is ever reached with a mismatched pair. pa_kv_cache_reorder_ref.cl
# itself (and its pa_kv_cache_reorder_ref.cm CM counterpart) are UNCHANGED - the guard is added at
# the one call site that can see both precisions, upstream of kernel compilation.
#
# ---- 11. THE THIRD UNIT TEST (fable-review follow-up F7) ----
